## 📌 Project Overview & Clinical Objective
This repository contains an end-to-end, automated machine learning classification pipeline engineered to predict patient stroke occurrences utilizing critical health indicators (such as age, average blood glucose spikes, and body mass index). 

In medical predictive analytics, handling severe data skew is a critical challenge. Within this clinical dataset, stroke occurrences account for a rare minority distribution of only **4.85%** (249 occurrences), while non-stroke records represent **95.15%** (4,869 occurrences). This architecture scales and evaluates six diverse baseline classifiers alongside two complex ensemble models, isolating the safest mathematical configuration for diagnostic risk containment.

