## 🛠️ Pipeline Methodology & Data Integrity
To replicate professional medical application deployment and guarantee structural validity, data preparation enforces strict data leakage barriers:

1. **Stratified Splitting First:** The dataset feature space was partitioned into three distinct blocks *prior* to any scaling or sampling operations: **Training (70%)**, **Validation (15%)**, and **Test (15%)**. 
2. **Feature Processing Pipeline:** Numerical indicators were standard-scaled around zero-mean variance boundaries, missing BMI records were imputed utilizing data-confined regional medians, and nominal factors were mapped via One-Hot Encoding expansion.
3. **SMOTE Balancing Safeguard:** To prevent majority-class classification bias, Synthetic Minority Over-sampling (SMOTE) was executed. Crucially, SMOTE operations were restricted *strictly* to the training matrix (`X_train_balanced`). Both evaluation matrices (Validation and Test) remained completely raw and un-SMOTEd to reflect authentic real-world emergency room class distributions.

